From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:38:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ec/lenovo/pmh7: Power the dGPU up with the PCIe timing

The PCI Express CEM specification wants the power rails stable for at
least 100 ms before PERST# goes high (T_PVPERL), and the PCI Express
Base specification 100 ms from the end of a reset to the first
configuration request. pmh7_dgpu_power_enable() waited 10 ms and 50 ms.
The _ON method of the dGPU power resource of the Lenovo Haswell boards
already waits 100 ms both times; do the same.

TEST=Built for Lenovo ThinkPad W541.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/ec/lenovo/pmh7/pmh7.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ec/lenovo/pmh7/pmh7.c b/src/ec/lenovo/pmh7/pmh7.c
index 00d34edb..ad8dfc48 100644
--- a/src/ec/lenovo/pmh7/pmh7.c
+++ b/src/ec/lenovo/pmh7/pmh7.c
@@ -56,9 +56,11 @@ void pmh7_dgpu_power_enable(int onoff)
 	if (onoff) {
 		pmh7_register_clear_bit(0x50, 7); // DGPU_RST
 		pmh7_register_set_bit(0x50, 3); // DGPU_PWR
-		mdelay(10);
+		/* PCIe CEM: power stable for 100 ms before PERST# goes high */
+		mdelay(100);
 		pmh7_register_set_bit(0x50, 7); // DGPU_RST
-		mdelay(50);
+		/* PCIe: 100 ms from the end of the reset to config requests */
+		mdelay(100);
 	} else {
 		pmh7_register_clear_bit(0x50, 7); // DGPU_RST
 		udelay(100);
-- 
